; Leg GP -- the host SENDS.  CKPRE (HEAD BEFORE section 1f, md5 537486a8)
; RECEIVES 32 KB at 38400.
;
; THE CONTROL SS16aj's SHEET SHOULD HAVE HAD.  SS16ak's three clean receive
; legs did 37,557 wire bytes in 31.137 / 31.143 / 31.535 s; SS16ah leg BC
; did the identical 37,557 in 28.057 s.  That is +11%, eight times that
; sitting's own 398 ms spread -- but a CROSS-SITTING comparison, which
; SS16aj itself says not to make.  GP and GQ make it a within-sitting one.
;
; PASS is simply a clean leg: rxlost=0 rxfull=0, 18 packets, 0 resends,
; 0 timeouts, 37,557 wire bytes, byte-exact.  The RESULT is the host clock,
; read against GQ and against nothing else.
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16alGP.pkt
send rcvgp.dat
statistics
